# FADE / RAMP edge cases for the note highway renderer.
# Verify with:  python _verify_highway_fade.py -s _fade_edge_cases.echoes 0 1500 3000 5000 7000 9000 11000
#
# LED 1  – slow fade (50 %/s) with no successor: tail runs off the look-ahead
# LED 2  – fast fade (99 %/s) re-triggered every half beat
# LED 3  – fade that is already black before "now" is reached
# LED 4  – two identical SET commands at the same instant (must not stack alpha)
# LED 5  – fade of a dim colour, no preceding SET
# LED 6  – SET immediately followed by a fade on a grey
# LED 7  – bright fade that reaches black inside the visible window
# LED 8  – dim fade, decays below one unit within a second
# LED 9  – ramp longer than the 2-beat look-ahead (gradient must not stretch)
# LED 10 – ramp that is cut short by another command (no stale hold)
# LED 11 – ramp exactly ending on a SET (no doubled alpha at the seam)
# LED 12 – ramp to black followed by a hold-colour ramp
0:00.000  SET 255 0 0  1
0:00.000  FADE 255 0 0 50  1
0:02.000  SET 0 0 255  2
0:02.000  FADE 0 0 255 99  2
0:02.214  SET 0 0 255  2
0:02.214  FADE 0 0 255 99  2
0:03.000  SET 0 255 0  3
0:03.000  FADE 0 255 0 99  3
0:03.500  SET 0 255 0  4
0:03.500  SET 0 255 0  4
0:04.000  FADE 120 60 30 90  5
0:05.000  SET 200 200 200  6
0:05.200  FADE 200 200 200 99  6
0:06.000  SET 255 255 255  7
0:06.100  FADE 255 255 255 99  7
0:07.000  SET 10 10 10  8
0:07.000  FADE 10 10 10 99  8
0:08.000  RAMP 0:02  255 0 0  0 0 255  9
0:11.000  RAMP 0:02  0 255 0  255 255 0  10
0:11.500  SET 200 0 0  10
0:13.000  RAMP 0:01  255 0 0  0 0 255  11
0:14.000  SET 0 255 0  11
0:15.000  RAMP 0:01  0 0 0  200 200 0  12
0:16.000  RAMP 0:01  200 200 0  10 200 60  12
